<title>BRAZIL: Brazil central bank sells dollar-indexed notes.</title>
<headline>Brazil central bank sells dollar-indexed notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's central bank on Wednesday sold dollar-indexed national treasury notes (NTN-D) for a total face value of 400 million reais.</p>
<p>The notes, which were part of the central bank's portfolio, come due on April 1, 1998, and pay an annual yield of 11.34 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 2485418))</p>
